We have supported a minority government led by the Center Party under Chancellor Joseph Wirth.



@no_majority_papen
on-arrival: pro_republic -= 10; next_election_time = time+3; next_election_month = month + 3; next_election_year = year; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; workers_nsdap += 6; unemployed_nsdap += 6; old_middle_nsdap += 5; new_middle_nsdap += 5; rural_nsdap += 5; no_majority_papen_elections += 1; workers_spd -= 8 if pro_republic < 45; workers_spd *= 0.85 if pro_republic < 40; workers_nsdap += 5 if pro_republic < 40;

After the elections, Papen is still deeply unpopular, without any hint of coalition support, and there is a vote of no confidence called against him almost immediately. No matter how we vote, the measure would pass. The Reichstag is dissolved once more.

