@no_majority_papen_2
on-arrival: chancellor = "Schleicher"; pro_republic -= 10; next_election_time = time+5; next_election_month = month + 5; next_election_year = year; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; workers_nsdap += 5; unemployed_nsdap += 10; old_middle_nsdap += 5; new_middle_nsdap += 5; rural_nsdap += 10; workers_spd -= 8 if pro_republic < 45; workers_spd *= 0.85 if pro_republic < 40; workers_nsdap += 5 if pro_republic < 40; finance_minister_party = "I"; interior_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "I"; foreign_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister_party = "I"; reichswehr_minister = "I";

There is no path to a majority government. Hindenburg is displeased with Papen, and calls on him to resign. Now, former army general Kurt von Schleicher has been appointed chancellor, again as part of a presidential government.

Schleicher's government is deeply unpopular among all parties of the Reichstag. Despite his support for a coalition with the NSDAP, the Nazis want power all to themselves, without Schleicher.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].


@no_majority_schleicher
